WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.139 --> 00:00:20.041
morning Sophie helped me dress, but she took so long that Mr.

2
00:00:20.081 --> 00:00:24.923
Rochester grew impatient and sent up a note asking why I was delayed.

3
00:00:26.044 --> 00:00:31.487
I hurried away from Sophie as soon as she finished attaching my veil—the plain lace one that I

4
00:00:31.527 --> 00:00:33.068
had originally intended to wear.

5
00:00:34.244 --> 00:00:35.804
"Lingerer!" said Mr.

6
00:00:35.865 --> 00:00:38.525
Rochester, meeting me at the foot of the stairs.

7
00:00:38.545 --> 00:00:43.126
"My brain is on fire with impatience, and you tarry so long."

8
00:00:44.247 --> 00:00:49.628
He took me into the dining room, where he looked me up and down, pronounced me "fair as

9
00:00:49.688 --> 00:00:53.329
a lily," and told me I had only ten minutes to eat breakfast.

10
00:00:54.549 --> 00:00:56.590
When I had finished, I rose from the table.

11
00:00:57.630 --> 00:01:03.252
There were no groomsmen, no bridesmaids, no relatives to gather, no one but Mr.

12
00:01:03.312 --> 00:01:04.704
Rochester and I.

13
00:01:05.885 --> 00:01:08.447
Mrs. Fairfax stood in the hall as we passed.

14
00:01:09.648 --> 00:01:12.229
I would gladly have spoken to her, but Mr.

15
00:01:12.289 --> 00:01:14.851
Rochester held my hand in an iron grip.

16
00:01:16.072 --> 00:01:18.854
I was hurried along by a stride that I could hardly match.

17
00:01:20.715 --> 00:01:24.217
I wondered what other bridegroom had ever looked so grimly resolute.

18
00:01:25.498 --> 00:01:28.680
The old gray church was just beyond the gates of Thornfield.

19
00:01:29.808 --> 00:01:30.968
At the churchyard Mr.

20
00:01:31.028 --> 00:01:34.309
Rochester realized I was out of breath, so we paused.

21
00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:39.171
I noticed two strangers walking among the headstones, but Mr.

22
00:01:39.211 --> 00:01:43.732
Rochester, who was staring earnestly at my face, did not see the men.

23
00:01:44.952 --> 00:01:49.114
When I felt rested, he gently walked me into the church and down the aisle.

24
00:01:50.314 --> 00:01:54.015
The two strangers loitered at the back of the church while the minister, Mr.

25
00:01:54.055 --> 00:01:56.876
Wood, and his clerk waited for us at the front.

26
00:01:57.972 --> 00:02:02.916
The wedding service began, and we reached the point where the clergyman asks the bride and groom if

27
00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:06.939
they know of any reason why they may not be lawfully joined in matrimony.

28
00:02:08.079 --> 00:02:10.241
Mr. Wood paused, as is the custom.

29
00:02:11.422 --> 00:02:14.024
When is that pause ever broken by a reply?

30
00:02:15.825 --> 00:02:19.487
Mr. Wood opened his mouth to continue, but he was interrupted.

31
00:02:19.508 --> 00:02:22.249
"The marriage cannot go on!

32
00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:25.492
I declare the existence of an impediment."

33
00:02:26.592 --> 00:02:28.953
The clergyman and his clerk looked at the speaker.

34
00:02:30.133 --> 00:02:37.815
Mr. Rochester rocked slightly, as if an earthquake had rolled under his feet, and said "Proceed" without turning

35
00:02:37.875 --> 00:02:39.156
his head or eyes.

36
00:02:39.176 --> 00:02:45.357
"I cannot proceed without some investigation into what has been asserted," said Mr.

37
00:02:45.397 --> 00:02:49.479
Wood. "What is the nature of this impediment?"

38
00:02:50.639 --> 00:02:53.720
Mr. Rochester made no motion except to take my hand.

39
00:02:54.932 --> 00:02:57.234
What a hot, strong grasp he had!

40
00:02:58.415 --> 00:03:03.099
The speaker approached the altar rail and said slowly in a low voice, "Mr.

41
00:03:03.179 --> 00:03:05.501
Rochester has a wife who is still living."

42
00:03:06.722 --> 00:03:11.986
My nerves vibrated to these soft-spoken words as they had never vibrated to thunder.

43
00:03:13.887 --> 00:03:14.668
I looked at Mr.

44
00:03:14.728 --> 00:03:17.210
Rochester and made him look at me.

45
00:03:18.391 --> 00:03:22.234
His whole face was a colorless rock; he seemed defiant.

46
00:03:23.335 --> 00:03:27.982
Without speaking, he wrapped his arm around my waist and pulled me to his side.

47
00:03:28.002 --> 00:03:30.223
"Who are you?"

48
00:03:30.624 --> 00:03:31.684
he asked the intruder.

49
00:03:31.704 --> 00:03:35.106
"And who is this wife you would thrust upon me?"

50
00:03:35.126 --> 00:03:39.269
"My name is Briggs, and I'm a London solicitor."

51
00:03:40.509 --> 00:03:43.091
He removed a paper from his pocket and began reading.

52
00:03:44.292 --> 00:03:51.516
I affirm that fifteen years ago Edward Fairfax Rochester married my sister, Bertha Mason, in Jamaica.

53
00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:55.702
A copy of the church record of that marriage is in my possession.

54
00:03:56.963 --> 00:03:58.824
Signed, Richard Mason.

55
00:03:58.844 --> 00:04:04.647
"That only proves that I've been married, not that my wife is still living," said Mr.

56
00:04:04.687 --> 00:04:09.370
Rochester. The second stranger stepped out of the shadows.

57
00:04:10.510 --> 00:04:11.751
It was Richard Mason.

58
00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:14.413
"She is living at Thornfield.

59
00:04:15.533 --> 00:04:16.934
I saw her there in April."

60
00:04:16.954 --> 00:04:19.796
"Impossible!" said the minister.

61
00:04:21.104 --> 00:04:24.126
"I'm a long-time resident here, and I've never heard of a Mrs.

62
00:04:24.246 --> 00:04:25.847
Rochester at Thornfield."

63
00:04:26.988 --> 00:04:29.089
I saw a grim smile contort Mr.

64
00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:34.393
Rochester's lips as he muttered, "No, I took care that none should hear of her under that name."

65
00:04:35.634 --> 00:04:39.236
He mused for a few minutes and then suddenly announced that there would be no wedding.

66
00:04:39.256 --> 00:04:41.157
"You say, Mr.

67
00:04:41.198 --> 00:04:42.799
Wood, that you've never heard of a Mrs.

68
00:04:42.899 --> 00:04:45.801
Rochester at Thornfield," he went on recklessly.

69
00:04:45.821 --> 00:04:50.624
"But I daresay you've heard gossip about a mysterious lunatic kept there.

70
00:04:51.864 --> 00:04:55.825
She is my wife, Bertha Mason, whom I married fifteen years ago.

71
00:04:57.766 --> 00:05:03.547
Bertha is insane, and she comes from an insane family, which I only discovered after I married her."

72
00:05:04.688 --> 00:05:07.088
He looked at me as he continued with his tale.

73
00:05:08.249 --> 00:05:10.729
"Jane knew nothing of this disgusting secret.

74
00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:13.730
She thought everything was fair and legal.

75
00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:17.731
Now I invite you all to come up to the house and visit Mrs.

76
00:05:17.811 --> 00:05:20.112
Poole's patient and my wife!

77
00:05:21.332 --> 00:05:24.274
You shall see what sort of being I was cheated into marrying."

78
00:05:25.474 --> 00:05:29.357
Still holding me tightly, he left the church with the other men following.

79
00:05:30.557 --> 00:05:32.598
I was too shocked to feel anything.

80
00:05:33.759 --> 00:05:35.100
As we entered the house, Mrs.

81
00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:38.782
Fairfax, Adele, and Sophie advanced to greet us, but Mr.

82
00:05:38.842 --> 00:05:41.703
Rochester swept past them and up to the third floor.

83
00:05:42.884 --> 00:05:45.085
He led us into the room where I had nursed Mr.

84
00:05:45.125 --> 00:05:49.908
Mason and lifted a tapestry there to reveal the other door, which he unlocked.

85
00:05:51.732 --> 00:05:57.954
Grace Poole bent over the fire, apparently cooking something, while a figure ran back and forth in the

86
00:05:57.994 --> 00:05:59.814
shadows at the far end of the room.

87
00:05:59.834 --> 00:06:01.535
"Good morning.

88
00:06:02.815 --> 00:06:04.116
How is your charge today?"

89
00:06:04.516 --> 00:06:05.016
asked Mr.

90
00:06:05.076 --> 00:06:10.437
Rochester. "Rather snappish, but not outrageous," replied Grace.

91
00:06:11.698 --> 00:06:17.539
At this the strange figure bellowed and brushed the hair away from her face, and I recognized the

92
00:06:17.559 --> 00:06:19.820
mysterious woman who had torn my veil.

93
00:06:21.068 --> 00:06:23.149
"We should leave her," Mason whispered.

94
00:06:23.169 --> 00:06:26.070
"Beware!" shouted Grace.

95
00:06:27.311 --> 00:06:28.871
Suddenly the woman rushed at Mr.

96
00:06:28.931 --> 00:06:32.513
Rochester, and they struggled as she tried to strangle and bite him.

97
00:06:33.733 --> 00:06:38.655
At last he managed to grab her arms, and with Grace's assistance, he tied her to a chair.

98
00:06:38.675 --> 00:06:42.437
"This is my wife," Mr.

99
00:06:42.497 --> 00:06:44.058
Rochester said breathlessly.

100
00:06:44.078 --> 00:06:46.739
"Off with you now.

101
00:06:48.059 --> 00:06:49.380
I must shut up my prize."

102
00:06:50.620 --> 00:06:52.361
As we descended the stairs, Mr.

103
00:06:52.401 --> 00:06:54.361
Briggs, the solicitor, addressed me.

104
00:06:55.521 --> 00:06:57.102
"You are clear of all blame, miss.

105
00:06:58.242 --> 00:07:01.063
Your uncle will be glad to hear that this marriage has been prevented."

106
00:07:02.183 --> 00:07:02.763
"My uncle?"

107
00:07:03.104 --> 00:07:04.064
I said in surprise.

108
00:07:04.084 --> 00:07:05.904
"Do you know him?"

109
00:07:05.924 --> 00:07:08.005
"Mr. Mason does.

110
00:07:09.165 --> 00:07:13.026
He happened to be staying with John Eyre in Madeira before returning to Jamaica.

111
00:07:14.207 --> 00:07:18.948
When your letter arrived announcing your marriage, Mason explained the true state of affairs.

112
00:07:20.304 --> 00:07:24.667
I'm sorry to say your uncle is now on his deathbed, so he urged Mason to hurry back

113
00:07:24.727 --> 00:07:25.227
to England."

114
00:07:26.548 --> 00:07:28.390
By this time we had reached my room.

115
00:07:29.510 --> 00:07:31.632
I shut myself in and fastened the lock.

116
00:07:32.913 --> 00:07:39.057
Still too stunned to weep or mourn, I mechanically removed the wedding dress and replaced it with my

117
00:07:39.137 --> 00:07:39.777
plain dress.

118
00:07:40.978 --> 00:07:42.019
My hopes were dead.

119
00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:49.424
Jane Eyre—who had almost been a bride—was a cold, solitary girl again.
